      "s6-c9-exempt",
      "Exempt Securities",
      "The '33 Act requires registration of nonexempt issues, such as corporate stocks, bonds, rights, warrants, options, investment companies, and variable insurance products.\n\nExempt issues fall into 4 groups:\n• Government issues: U.S. government debt, agency debt (such as Fannie Mae, Ginnie Mae, or Federal Home Loan Bank bonds), municipal debt, and foreign government debt.\n• Issuers already regulated by other laws: insurance company offerings (but not variable annuities or variable life), bank issues, and common carriers such as railroads and trucking companies.\n• Nonprofit issues: farmers' cooperatives and nonprofit educational or charitable groups.\n• Others: money market securities that mature in 270 days or less, and issues of small business investment companies.\n\nMunicipal securities do not register with the SEC and need no prospectus. Instead, they usually file an official statement with the Municipal Securities Rulemaking Board (MSRB) and give it to investors.",
